    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0588" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1199.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Livingston to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>
                            <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Cape Haitien</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rebels retreated in good order Saturday afternoon preceded by many women and
                    children and will probably continue revolution. Many refugees in consulates and
                    some aboard French cruiser. Detachments <pb facs="0589" n="473" xml:id="pg473"/>
                    of marines are guarding French Consulate, bank and bishopric. There were some
                    executions yesterday for pillaging.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Livingston</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
